// Simplified state/union-territory boundaries for India, embedded so the app
// never depends on a network fetch. 35 shapes cover the 28 states + 8 union
// territories: two pairs are drawn as a single combined shape because
// splitting them precisely would need far more detail than a study map
// needs —
//   - Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh share one outline (they were one state
//     until the 2019 reorganisation into two union territories).
//   - Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu are drawn as the single
//     merged union territory they have in fact been since 2020.
// Both are still quizzed as their real, separate seats of government.
