// A coarse relief layer, purely decorative: four elevation bands (200 m,
// 600 m, 1,500 m, 3,000 m) painted over the base map so the Himalaya, the
// Western and Eastern Ghats, and the Deccan plateau actually look like what
// they are instead of flat colour. There is no survey-grade DEM behind this
// -- the brief explicitly allows quantizing -- just ~170 hand-placed control
// points at well-documented peaks, plateaus, valleys, and plains, blended
// with k-nearest-neighbour inverse-distance weighting (plain global IDW badly
// over-smoothed sharp transitions -- the Assam valley came out reading
// 900 m+ because it sits near enough to the Naga hills), thresholded,
// smoothed, and clipped to this file's own state outlines so the tint never
// spills past a coastline the border layer doesn't draw.
